# Build outputs
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
*.asi
!examples/**/*.asi  # keep examples if any
*.dll
!vendor/**/*.dll
!examples/**/*.dll  # example plugin DLLs ship via release zips
*.exe
*.pdb
*.exp
*.lib
*.obj
*.o
*.a
# Compiled Java from the vendored BLAKE3 self-test (javac output; regenerated
# from the tracked .java sources by the run recipe in Blake3SelfTest.java).
*.class

# IDE / tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Logs
*.log

# Local artifacts not for source control
# _download/ — cached downloads (ULAH zip etc.); regenerated by build/release scripts
# release-staging/ — generated drag-drop release; produced by release scripts
# test-install/ — local staging area used when iterating against the live game
_download/
release-staging/
test-install/

# Private working materials are TRACKED on `main` (→ private remote) and STRIPPED
# when projecting `main` → `public` by publish-public.ps1. They are NOT gitignored
# anymore — the private/public split is enforced at publish time, not by ignore.
# See publish-public.ps1 for the authoritative sanitize set.
#
# What stays ignored below is only genuinely heavy / reproducible binaries inside
# the otherwise-tracked private trees, so the private repo holds the scripts and
# notes without carrying gigabytes of third-party toolchain.

# third-party-ghidra/: track the scripts + README; ignore the toolchain binaries
# and the multi-GB analyzed project DB (clone-and-go expects these present locally).
third-party-ghidra/ghidra_project/
third-party-ghidra/ghidra_12.1_PUBLIC/
third-party-ghidra/x64dbg/
third-party-ghidra/ninja/
third-party-ghidra/WHGame.dll
third-party-ghidra/*.fidb

# test-fixtures/: track the probe sources + manifests; ignore built .pak blobs.
test-fixtures/pak-mods/**/*.pak

# _research/: tracked (recon notes, scripts, wiki cache). Predecessor-sig clones
# are shallow clones of third-party repos — keep them on disk, out of git.
_research/predecessor-sigs/